  help: `filesystem` takes only its filesystem name

  x unknown node `var-disk` in install
   ,-[tests/repos/broken-layout/repo.kdl:7:13]
 6 |             filesystem "xfs" subvolumes=#true pool="rpool"
 7 |             var-disk "sdb"
   :             ^^^^|^^^
   :                 `-- not part of the schema
 8 |         }
   `----
  help: an install block accepts `filesystem`, `composefs`, `generic-image`,
        `admin-group` and `bootloader`

  x `zfs` is not a filesystem the installer formats
    ,-[tests/repos/broken-layout/repo.kdl:12:13]
 11 |         install {
 12 |             filesystem "zfs"
    :             ^^^^^|^^^^
    :                  `-- not a filesystem
 13 |             composefs #true
    `----
  help: the installer auto-partitions `xfs`, `ext4` and `btrfs`

  x `sealed` declares an install block, and nothing in the image provides
  | `bootc`
   ,-[tests/repos/broken-layout/repo.kdl:5:9]
 4 |     sealed {
 5 |         install {
   :         ^^^|^^^
   :            `-- a bootc-only node
 6 |             filesystem "xfs" subvolumes=#true pool="rpool"
   `----
  help: an install block describes how bootc installs the image: use a base
        that provides `bootc`, or drop `install`

  x `sealed` names no bootloader
   ,-[tests/repos/broken-layout/repo.kdl:5:9]
 4 |     sealed {
 5 |         install {
   :         ^^^|^^^
   :            `-- no bootloader
 6 |             filesystem "xfs" subvolumes=#true pool="rpool"
   `----
  help: no family answers the bootloader: `bootloader "grub2"` here, from
        those the base component lists

  x `sealed` installs a sealed deployment onto xfs
   ,-[tests/repos/broken-layout/repo.kdl:5:9]
 4 |     sealed {
 5 |         install {
   :         ^^^|^^^
   :            `-- xfs has no fs-verity
 6 |             filesystem "xfs" subvolumes=#true pool="rpool"
   `----
  help: the `debian` family installs with the composefs backend, which needs
        fs-verity: declare `ext4` or `btrfs`, or drop `filesystem` and take
        the family's own

  x `halfway` declares an install block, and nothing in the image provides
  | `bootc`
    ,-[tests/repos/broken-layout/repo.kdl:11:9]
 10 |     halfway {
 11 |         install {
    :         ^^^|^^^
    :            `-- a bootc-only node
 12 |             filesystem "zfs"
    `----
  help: an install block describes how bootc installs the image: use a base
        that provides `bootc`, or drop `install`

  x `halfway` declares half an install block
    ,-[tests/repos/broken-layout/repo.kdl:11:9]
 10 |     halfway {
 11 |         install {
    :         ^^^|^^^
    :            `-- no generic-image, admin-group, bootloader
 12 |             filesystem "zfs"
    `----
  help: nothing here has measured how `arch` installs, so this build answers
        for itself: an `install` block naming all of `filesystem`,
        `composefs`, `generic-image`, `admin-group` and `bootloader` builds
        install media, and no `install` block builds none
